# Example 26: Cello-style closed-loop design automation (S4)
# A truth table ("y = NOT(a)") is compiled end to end into a full
# synthetic biology design package, mirroring the Cello workflow
# (Nielsen et al. 2016 Science 352:aac7341; Cello 2.0, Jones et al.
# 2022 Nat Protoc 17:1097):
#
#   1. truth table -> minimized Boolean netlist
#   2. characterized gate assignment (Hill transfer scoring)
#   3. gate DNA assembly
#   4. full plasmid + GenBank (synbio_designer backbone parts)
#   5. SBOL3 export for SynBioHub/Cello/LOICA interoperability
#   6. predicted dynamics (iterated transfer functions) and simulated
#      expression time curves (coupled transcription-translation)
#
# The closed loop validates that the *predicted* truth table matches
# the *target* truth table before the design is handed to a wet lab.
#
#gene name=gate_output
ATG GCT GGT GTA TAA
#end
#
#config library=pUC19 marker=AmpR output=stdout
